---
// The design system, as a page of the site itself: principles, colours (drawn
// from the real tokens), type, shape, marks and the posts kit. Dev only: it is
// the reference while the redesign is built, not part of the site.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

if (import.meta.env.PROD) return Astro.redirect("/");
---

<Base
  title="Design system · Colin Cheung"
  description="The design system for colincheung.dev."
>
  <div class="ds">
    <div class="top">
      <span>colincheung.dev · design system</span>
      <span class="f">the theme button is in the nav</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Grey does the structure. The accent points.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The one reference for how the site looks, drawn with the site's own tokens
      and fonts. Dark is the default; light is a soft toggle. The colours come
      from <code>docs/redesign/comps/tokens.mts</code>; when a decision changes,
      this page changes in the same commit. What was tried and dropped lives in
      <code>docs/design-rejected.md</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <p>What every decision comes back to.</p>
    <ol class="princ">
      <li>
        <b>One thing per glance.</b>
        The name leads; one thing moves on the first screen; one accent, used
        sparingly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Real over decorative.</b>
        Real numbers, live weather, real posts and roles. A slogan or a
        placeholder figure gets cut.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Personality in the content, not the chrome.</b>
        The one-liners, 張志權 and the homelab carry the character; surfaces
        stay grey and flat.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Light type.</b>
        Thin for the voice, semibold only for names. Anything that reads thick
        gets lighter.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>The terminal shows, it does not ask.</b>
        Real-looking commands with real output; nothing to type; nothing that
        repeats the page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Each fact once.</b>
        If it is in the hero, the CV or a post, it does not appear again.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Motion has a cause.</b>
        Slow, pauses on hover, off with reduced motion.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Fewer options.</b>
        Once a choice is made the comp loses the switch, and the dropped idea
        goes in the rejected list.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Colour</h2>
    <p>
      Three kinds of colour and nothing else: one grey scale, four accent
      shades, three status colours. Each is one OKLCH value; only lightness
      changes between light and dark, so dark mode is the same palette, not a
      second one.
    </p>
    <div class="scale">
      <h3>neutral · hue 255, barely tinted cool · 12 steps</h3>
      <div class="sw" data-sw="n"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="scale">
      <h3>accent · violet, hue 298 · four shades, one job each</h3>
      <div class="sw four" data-sw="a"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="scale">
      <h3>
        status · green ok, amber warn, red danger · steps 3 (wash), 9 (dot), 11
        (text) only
      </h3>
      <div class="sw three" data-sw="s"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>surfaces</h3>
        <p>dark (the default): page n1 · panel n3 · well n4</p>
        <p>
          light (the toggle): page n5 · panel n3 · figures and quotes n2 · well
          n4, no pure white
        </p>
        <p class="m">separated by tone, never by a shadow</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>text</h3>
        <p>ink = n12 · for titles and values</p>
        <p class="m">muted = n11 · the line under a title</p>
        <p class="f">faint = n10 · dates, labels, captions (4.5:1)</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>edges</h3>
        <p>line = ink at 10% · strong = 16% · faint = 5%</p>
        <p class="m">dark: white at the same alphas</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>accent · results and links</h3>
        <p class="stat">
          <span class="was">12 h →</span><b>11 min</b>
          <span class="f">the result, full violet</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/blog/">a link to the writing</a>
          <span class="f">where it goes</span>
        </p>
        <p class="f">
          plus the one highlight in a hero drawing, and a control under the
          pointer. Never chrome (prompts, carets, window dots, the nav,
          separators), a surface, a heading or a button. It also stands for
          "info": there is no separate blue status colour.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>status · traffic lights, small</h3>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:0">
          <span class="badge badge--ok"><i></i>live</span
          ><span class="badge badge--warn"><i></i>draft</span
          ><span class="badge badge--danger"><i></i>down</span>
        </div>
        <p class="f" style="margin-top:.6rem">
          dots and small badges only; always with a word, never colour alone
          (amber fills are under 3:1 on white everywhere). Red appears only for
          a real failure, such as a homelab service down; a result that got
          worse stays ink.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>controls are ink</h3>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:0">
          <a class="btn btn--ink" href="/blog/jest-to-vitest/">Read the post</a
          ><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/cv/">CV</a
          ><span class="ico"
            ><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path
                d="M12 .5C5.7.5.5 5.7.5 12c0 5.1 3.3 9.4 7.9 10.9.6.1.8-.2.8-.6v-2c-3.2.7-3.9-1.4-3.9-1.4-.5-1.3-1.3-1.7-1.3-1.7-1-.7.1-.7.1-.7 1.2.1 1.8 1.2 1.8 1.2 1 1.8 2.7 1.3 3.4 1 .1-.8.4-1.3.7-1.6-2.6-.3-5.3-1.3-5.3-5.7 0-1.3.5-2.3 1.2-3.1-.1-.3-.5-1.5.1-3.1 0 0 1-.3 3.2 1.2a11 11 0 0 1 5.8 0c2.2-1.5 3.2-1.2 3.2-1.2.6 1.6.2 2.8.1 3.1.8.8 1.2 1.8 1.2 3.1 0 4.4-2.7 5.4-5.3 5.7.4.4.8 1.1.8 2.2v3.2c0 .3.2.7.8.6 4.6-1.5 7.9-5.8 7.9-10.9C23.5 5.7 18.3.5 12 .5z"
              />
            </svg></span
          >
        </div>
        <p class="f" style="margin-top:.6rem">
          black or outlined, 6px corners; no blue buttons, no pills
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Type</h2>
    <p>
      Sora for names and the voice, Geist for reading, DM Mono for data.
      Tracking tightens as size grows.
    </p>
    <div class="card type">
      <p class="t-name">Colin Cheung</p>
      <p class="t-mono">
        Sora 600 · −0.05em · the name, and section headings at 1.3rem
      </p>
      <p class="t-line" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
        still waiting to reverse a <b>linked list</b> at work
      </p>
      <p class="t-mono">
        Sora 200, punchline 400 · −0.03em · the one-liners and the worked-at
        names
      </p>
      <p class="t-title" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
        Part 3: How Jev performs on Aliens
      </p>
      <p class="t-mono">
        Geist 400 · post and list titles; never 500 or heavier in lists
      </p>
      <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:1rem">
        Body at 16–17px, line-height 1.55, muted when it sits under a title.
      </p>
      <p class="t-mono">Geist 400</p>
      <p class="t-mono" style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--ink)">
        $ top -u colin · 4.5 GB → 221 MB · Oct 27
      </p>
      <p class="t-mono">
        DM Mono 300–400 · the terminal, dates, stats, captions
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Shape and depth</h2>
    <p>
      Small, consistent corners and no shadows. Depth comes from tone: a white
      panel on a grey page, a darker well inside a panel.
    </p>
    <div class="shape">
      <div style="width:12rem;height:6rem;border-radius:var(--r)">
        8px<br>panels, cards, figures
      </div>
      <div
        style="width:8rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:var(--r-ctl);border:1px solid var(--line-strong)"
      >
        6px · controls
      </div>
      <div
        style="width:5rem;height:1.6rem;border-radius:var(--r-chip);background:var(--well)"
      >
        4px · chips
      </div>
      <div
        style="width:1.6rem;height:1.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--n6)"
        title="only dots are round"
      ></div>
    </div>
    <p class="f" style="margin-top:.8rem">
      Only dots are round. No pills, no 12px+ corners, no drop shadows, no
      gradients or glows; the one halo is the focus ring on the current dot.
    </p>

    <h2>Marks and motion</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>the slash</h3>
        <p>
          PodFather <span class="t-mono">2017</span
          ><span class="slash">/</span>Skyscanner
          <span class="t-mono">2020</span>
        </p>
        <p class="f">
          the separator and the "this one" marker, in the accent, Sora 200
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>status dot</h3>
        <p>
          <span class="dot" style="background:var(--ok9)"></span>observability
        </p>
        <p class="f">with its word, never alone</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>motion</h3>
        <p>
          one moving thing on the first screen (the one-liner, 5 s); figures
          move slowly; hover pauses; reduced motion stills everything
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Posts</h2>
    <p>
      Posts are most of the site, so they get the same rules plus a kit for
      figures. One column for everything: text, figures, code and tables share
      one measure (44rem) and one left edge; wider breakout figures were tried
      and dropped. Real posts reskinned in this system:
      <code>shots/42-*.png</code>.
    </p>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>layout</h3>
        <svg
          viewBox="0 0 220 120"
          style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block"
          aria-label="the post column"
        >
          <rect
            x="0"
            y="0"
            width="220"
            height="120"
            rx="6"
            fill="var(--well)"
          />
          <rect x="45" y="10" width="130" height="8" rx="2" fill="var(--n8)" />
          <rect
            x="45"
            y="24"
            width="60"
            height="6"
            rx="2"
            fill="var(--accent-solid)"
          />
          <rect x="45" y="38" width="130" height="3" fill="var(--n7)" />
          <rect x="45" y="45" width="120" height="3" fill="var(--n7)" />
          <rect
            x="45"
            y="56"
            width="130"
            height="30"
            rx="3"
            fill="var(--panel)"
          />
          <rect x="45" y="94" width="130" height="3" fill="var(--n7)" />
          <rect x="45" y="101" width="110" height="3" fill="var(--n7)" />
          <path d="M45 114H175" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
          <text
            x="110"
            y="118"
            font-size="6"
            text-anchor="middle"
            fill="var(--faint)"
            font-family="DM Mono"
          >
            44rem, one edge
          </text>
        </svg>
        <p class="f" style="margin-top:.6rem">
          a wide screen grows the type a little, never the line length; a
          reading-progress bar in the accent sits at the top
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>header</h3>
        <p class="t-mono" style="color:var(--accent)">// writing</p>
        <p
          style="font-family:var(--head);font-weight:600;font-size:1.35rem;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1.1;margin:.2rem 0 .7rem"
        >
          CI faster than GitHub's, for free
        </p>
        <p class="t-mono" style="margin:0">vs GitHub</p>
        <p
          style="font-family:var(--head);font-weight:600;font-size:1.6rem;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0"
        >
          <span style="color:var(--faint);font-weight:400">26 s</span>
          <span class="f" style="font-weight:300">→</span>
          <span style="color:var(--accent)">20 s</span>
        </p>
        <p class="t-mono">Oct 16, 2026 · 4 min read</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>prose</h3>
        <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0 0 .5rem">
          Geist 400 at 16–17px, line-height 1.65.
          <b style="font-weight:600">Bold</b>
          is 600.
          <a href="/blog/">Links</a>
          are the accent with a faint underline.
        </p>
        <p class="f" style="margin:0">
          each
          <span style="font-family:var(--head);font-weight:600;color:var(--ink)"
            >##</span
          >
          heading is Sora 600 with a hairline above it, so a long post scans as
          sections
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1.6rem">figure anatomy</h3>
    <figure
      class="card"
      style="margin:0;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)"
    >
      <p class="t-mono" style="margin:0 0 .7rem;font-size:11px">
        a short title above · 11px
      </p>
      <div
        style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:5rem 1fr 4rem;gap:.45rem .8rem;align-items:center;font-size:12.8px"
      >
        <span>GitHub</span
        ><i
          style="height:.55rem;background:var(--n7);border-radius:1px;display:block"
        ></i><b style="font-weight:500;text-align:right;color:var(--muted)"
          >26 s</b
        >
        <span style="color:var(--ink)">mini PC</span
        ><i
          style="height:.55rem;width:77%;background:var(--accent-solid);border-radius:1px;display:block"
        ></i><b style="font-weight:500;text-align:right;color:var(--accent)"
          >20 s</b
        >
      </div>
      <figcaption style="margin-top:.7rem;font-size:11px;color:var(--faint)">
        at most one line of caption below, for a note · labels on the marks at
        12.8px
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="f" style="margin-top:.6rem">
      One panel on the well tone, 8px, no border. Text in two sizes only, at any
      width: 11px for titles, ticks and notes; 12.8px for labels and values.
      Explanation goes in one sentence of prose, not under the chart.
    </p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1.6rem">chart palette</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p>
          <span
            class="dot"
            style="border-radius:1px;width:1.4rem;background:var(--n7)"
          ></span
          >baseline, before, the others
        </p>
        <p>
          <span
            class="dot"
            style="border-radius:1px;width:1.4rem;background:var(--accent-solid)"
          ></span
          >the result, the option kept, the post's subject
        </p>
        <p>
          <span
            class="dot"
            style="border-radius:1px;width:1.4rem;background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,var(--n7) 0 3px,transparent 3px 6px)"
          ></span
          >the baseline row, striped, always first
        </p>
        <p>
          <span
            class="dot"
            style="border-radius:1px;width:1.4rem;background:var(--n5)"
          ></span
          >an estimate, lighter
        </p>
        <p>
          <span
            style="display:inline-block;width:1.4rem;border-top:1px dashed var(--muted);margin-right:.4rem;vertical-align:.25em"
          ></span
          >a reference line, dashed, explained once
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>changes · the traffic lights</h3>
        <p>
          <b style="color:var(--ok11);font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500"
            >+3.1</b
          > <span class="f">a real gain</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <b
            style="color:var(--danger11);font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500"
            >−2.4</b
          > <span class="f">a real drop</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <b style="color:var(--faint);font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500"
            >+0.6</b
          > <span class="f">could be luck</span>
        </p>
        <p class="f">
          only on charts that compare runs, with a key on the chart; never the
          accent's job
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>every chart</h3>
        <p class="f" style="font-size:.9rem">
          a short title · axis titles with units, "win rate (%)" · the baseline
          first · numbers in their own aligned column · even row spacing · every
          mark explained once · fits at 375px with nothing scrolling sideways ·
          checked in both themes
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1.6rem">the kit · pick the form by the job</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>A vs B · bars to scale</h3>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 200 54" style="width:100%">
          <g font-family="DM Mono" font-size="8" fill="var(--muted)">
            <text x="0" y="13">Jest</text>
            <text x="0" y="33">Vitest</text>
            <text x="198" y="13" text-anchor="end">428 s</text>
            <text x="198" y="33" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--accent)">
              23 s
            </text>
          </g>
          <rect x="38" y="6" width="125" height="9" fill="var(--n7)" />
          <rect x="38" y="26" width="7" height="9" fill="var(--accent-solid)" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>options · dot plot on one axis</h3>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 200 54" style="width:100%">
          <path d="M50 50H190" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
          <g font-family="DM Mono" font-size="8" fill="var(--muted)">
            <text x="0" y="12">QEMU</text>
            <text x="0" y="26">Firecracker</text>
            <text x="0" y="40">Docker</text>
          </g>
          <circle cx="185" cy="9" r="3" fill="var(--n9)" />
          <circle cx="118" cy="23" r="3.4" fill="var(--accent-solid)" />
          <circle cx="104" cy="37" r="3" fill="var(--n9)" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>shares · one bar, split</h3>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 200 54" style="width:100%">
          <rect x="0" y="10" width="158" height="12" fill="var(--n7)" />
          <rect
            x="160"
            y="10"
            width="40"
            height="12"
            fill="var(--accent-solid)"
          />
          <g font-family="DM Mono" font-size="8" fill="var(--muted)">
            <text x="0" y="40">80% loading the engine</text>
            <text x="200" y="40" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--accent)">
              20% running
            </text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>over time · line</h3>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 200 70" style="width:100%">
          <path d="M20 60H196M20 6V60" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
          <path
            d="M24 56L80 44L120 36L192 12"
            stroke="var(--n8)"
            fill="none"
            stroke-width="1.5"
          />
          <path
            d="M24 58L80 57L120 57L192 56"
            stroke="var(--accent-solid)"
            fill="none"
            stroke-width="2"
          />
          <path d="M20 30H196" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
          <g font-family="DM Mono" font-size="7" fill="var(--faint)">
            <text x="196" y="68" text-anchor="end">test files →</text>
            <text x="2" y="10">min</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>where time goes · bridge</h3>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 200 64" style="width:100%">
          <g fill="var(--n7)">
            <rect x="40" y="2" width="150" height="8" />
            <rect x="176" y="14" width="14" height="8" />
            <rect x="128" y="26" width="48" height="8" />
          </g>
          <rect
            x="40"
            y="38"
            width="88"
            height="8"
            fill="var(--accent-solid)"
          />
          <g font-family="DM Mono" font-size="7.5" fill="var(--muted)">
            <text x="0" y="9">GitHub</text>
            <text x="0" y="21">pickup</text>
            <text x="0" y="33">installs</text>
            <text x="0" y="45" fill="var(--ink)">mini PC</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>time at a glance · a square a day</h3>
        <div
          data-days
          style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(20,1fr);gap:2px"
        ></div>
        <p class="t-mono" style="margin-top:.5rem;font-size:11px">
          60 days then · <span style="color:var(--accent)">9 days now</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="f" style="margin-top:.6rem">
      Also in the kit, each built as a component and drawn by the same rules:
      steps on a shared time axis, step charts for a run of improvements, trees
      and arrows for structure, recordings (pixelated, playing only while on
      screen), JSON and code panels. Never plain boxes with text in them.
    </p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1.6rem">blocks</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>code</h3>
        <pre
          style="margin:0;padding:.8rem 1rem;border-radius:var(--r);background:var(--n2);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink);overflow:auto"
        ><span style="color:var(--accent)">export default</span> defineConfig({"{"}
  test: {"{"} isolate: <span style="color:var(--accent)">false</span> {"}"},
{"}"});</pre>
        <p class="f" style="margin-top:.6rem">
          wrapped, never scrolling sideways; its highlighting theme set in the
          build
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>table · hairline rails</h3>
        <div
          style="font-size:.85rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:0"
        >
          <span
            class="t-mono"
            style="padding:.2rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-strong)"
            >claim</span
          ><span
            class="t-mono"
            style="padding:.2rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-strong);text-align:right"
            >£</span
          ><span style="padding:.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)"
            >compensation</span
          ><span
            class="stat"
            style="padding:.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:right"
